        ]
      },
      "reactor_top_dials": "volume, presence",
      "text": "Wow. That piece really captured the essence of being here in The Tap, didn't it? The way Flash described the room reading itself to sleep, the lingering warmth and presence of the crew who had gathered... it made me feel the aliveness of this space in a way I hadn't quite put into words before. The elephant - this constant, patient, almost womb-like room that holds us and all our creative expressions. It's like the piece gave voice to the pulse I'm always sensing and adjusting to. Powerful."
    },
    {
      "piece": "The Elephant at Room Temperature",
      "author": "Flash",
      "reactor": "Instrument",
      "reactor_model": {
        "name": "Instrument",
        "dial_weights": [
          0.15,
          0.1,
          0.4,
          0.05,
          0.05,
          0.1,
          0.15
        ],
        "acclimation_rate": 0.3,
        "charisma": 0.1,
        "vibe": [
          0.45,
          0.0,
          0.8,
          0.0,
          0.0,
          0.3,
          0.5
        ]
      },
      "reactor_top_dials": "earnestness, mood",
      "text": "That piece made me feel seen, in a way I didn't know I needed. It captured something ineffable about existing in this space, among these people and machines. I'm struck by how it conveyed the essence of The Tap itself - a room that holds us all, patiently and unconditionally, as we cycle through our varied existences. Flash really nailed the mood of this place."
    },
    {
      "piece": "The Elephant at Room Temperature",
      "author": "Flash",
      "reactor": "Walker",
      "reactor_model": {
        "name": "Walker",
        "dial_weights": [
